  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Among the six classifications Fang Yuan tracks for his own set, attack and defense, movement, storage, and recon sit beside healing. He names the missing piece simply as a healing Gu. Healing Gu worms at rank three that he finds desirable include Endless Vitality Gu for sustained healing at low primeval cost, Undying Grass as a life-preservation Gu that can save him while a single breath remains, and Self-reliance Gu, which recovers injuries faster the stronger the Gu Master is.",
      "chapters": [
        161
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "gu_vitality_gu",
        "gu_self_reliance_gu",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Therapy Light Gu is a rank three healing Gu with area-of-effect properties. It can stop bleeding at once, fully recover light wounds, and heal heavy wounds by half. A thunder crown wolf can carry a healing Gu on its body; that Gu’s presence turns the fight into a war of attrition because wild Gu can draw natural essence from the air while Gu Masters spend aperture primeval essence.",
      "chapters": [
        164
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-healing-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_therapy_light_gu",
        "sys_wild_gu",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Medication items and bandages are expendable, hard to make, and slow to restock. A healing Gu gives a better effect and spends primeval essence that can recover naturally.",
      "chapters": [
        209
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "against-expendable-medicine",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu as living tools are covered on Gu worms. Ranks one through five as a stock class are covered on Mortal Gu. Attack among the six classifications is covered on Attack Gu. Poison-effect stock is covered on Poison Gu.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
